Subject: [PATCH] wave: remove the CCMP ICV before delivering management frames

The generic firmware BSS receive path retains both the CCMP header and ICV.
Removing only the header leaves eight bytes after the management body. In
particular, an FT-over-DS request then reaches hostapd with an invalid trailing
information element and is rejected before authentication can complete.

Remove both fields before AP cfg80211 or STA mac80211 delivery. This also
satisfies the existing RX_FLAG_IV_STRIPPED contract, which includes the ICV.
Keep the WEP authentication and group/BIP paths unchanged. Firmware-handled
Block Ack frames use a separate normalization path.

--- a/wireless/driver/shared/frame.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/shared/frame.c
@@ -627,16 +627,19 @@
     }
     else {
       if (mtlk_vap_is_ap(core->vap_handle) || !is_multicast_ether_addr(head->dst_addr.au8Addr)) {
-        if (flen < IEEE80211_CCMP_HEADER_LEN) {
+        if (flen < IEEE80211_CCMP_HEADER_LEN + IEEE80211_CCMP_MIC_LEN) {
           ILOG1_D("CID-%04x: Management Frame length is wrong", mtlk_vap_get_oid(core->vap_handle));
           res = MTLK_ERR_NOT_IN_USE;
           goto end;
         }
-        /* Remove security header from managment frames with decreasing the length */
+        /* Generic BSS RX retains the authenticated CCMP header and ICV.
+         * Deliver only the plaintext management body to both consumers;
+         * IV_STRIPPED makes mac80211 skip its own CCMP trailer removal.
+         */
         mtlk_dump(3, head, *buflen, "dump of man frame with security header");
-        flen -= IEEE80211_CCMP_HEADER_LEN;
-        *buflen -= IEEE80211_CCMP_HEADER_LEN;
+        flen -= IEEE80211_CCMP_HEADER_LEN + IEEE80211_CCMP_MIC_LEN;
+        *buflen -= IEEE80211_CCMP_HEADER_LEN + IEEE80211_CCMP_MIC_LEN;
         memmove(fbuf, fbuf + IEEE80211_CCMP_HEADER_LEN, flen);
           fd->pmf_flags |= MTLK_MGMT_FRAME_DECRYPTED;
           fd->pmf_flags |= MTLK_MGMT_FRAME_IV_STRIPPED;
       }
